 470, 25362, 198, 13874, 19324, 1986, 2038, 38919, 264, 18929, 12111, 311, 29436, 279, 9892, 323, 11900, 72, 315, 25362, 369, 2664, 35713, 15024, 13, 576, 17042, 729, 66249, 1246, 1632, 1817, 12671, 18304, 2878, 279, 4982, 9334, 2041, 49817, 11, 448, 5080, 2750, 18860, 2664, 35713, 13, 576, 2856, 7042, 374, 7907, 26618, 11, 323, 279, 18929, 12111, 5367, 7887, 34950, 279, 7042, 916, 5248, 21787, 553, 26301, 6562, 3118, 389, 862, 17042, 12205, 323, 6825, 45371, 1526, 48380, 7525, 13], "created_at": "2026-10-28T12:11:22.154612864Z", "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "eval_count": 701, "eval_duration": 136335666135, "load_duration": 148181124, "model": "qwen2.5:3b", "prompt_eval_count": 1220, "prompt_eval_duration": 61247191240, "response": "```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\n\ndef pack_circles(n: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Pack n circles in a unit square to maximize the sum of radii.\n    \n    Args:\n        n: Number of circles to pack\n    \n    Returns:\n        Numpy array of shape (n, 3) where each row is (x, y, radius)\n        All values should be between 0 and 1\n        Circles must not overlap\n        \n    Important: Set \"all\" random seeds to 2025, including the packages (such as scipy sub-packages) involving random seeds.\n    \n    Changed mechanism: Instead of using simulated annealing with exponential cooling, this function employs a local search approach combined with a genetic algorithm for better packing efficiency. The genetic algorithm iteratively improves the positions and radii of circles to maximize their sum while ensuring no overlap.\n    \"\"\"\n    np.random.seed(2025)\n    if n == 0:\n        return np.zeros((0, 3))\n    \n    # Initialize random positions and radii for each circle\n    points = qmc.Sobol(n=n*n, seed=2025).random(n)\n    circles = np.zeros((n, 3))\n    circles[:, :2] = points\n    \n    # Genetic algorithm to optimize the positions and radii of circles\n    def fitness(circles):\n        for i in range(n):\n            x, y, r = circles[i]\n            if not all(np.sqrt((circles[j,0]-x)**2 + (circles[j,1]-y)**2) > 2*r for j in range(i)):\n                return -np.sum(r)\n        return -np.sum(r)\n    \n    # Initial population of circles\n    def initial_population(n):\n        return np.random.uniform(0, 1, size=(n, 3))\n    \n    # Genetic algorithm function to optimize the positions and radii of circles\n    def genetic_algorithm(population):\n        for _ in range(50):  # Number of generations\n            fitness_values = np.array([fitness(circle) for circle in population])\n            indices = np.argsort(fitness_values)\n            new_population = initial_population(n)\n            \n            for i, idx in enumerate(indices[:int(len(indices)/2)]):\n                parent1_idx = indices[i]\n                parent2_idx = indices[i+1]\n                \n                parent1 = population[parent1_idx]\n                parent2 = population[parent2_idx]\n                \n                child1 = np.clip(parent1 + 0.5 * (parent2 - parent1), 0, 1)\n                child2 = np.clip(parent2 + 0.5 * (parent1 - parent2), 0, 1)\n                \n                new_population[i] = child1\n                new_population[i+1] = child2\n            \n            population = new_population\n    \n        return population\n    \n    # Genetic algorithm optimization\n    circles = genetic_algorithm(initial_population(n))\n    \n    return circles\n```\n\nThis code introduces a genetic algorithm to optimize the positions and radii of circles for better packing efficiency. The fitness function evaluates how well each circle fits within the unit square without overlapping, with higher values indicating better packing. The initial population is generated randomly, and the genetic algorithm iteratively improves the population over multiple generations by selecting parents based on their fitness scores and creating offspring through crossover operations.", "total_duration": 199556182923}}, "revisionId": "regional-prompt-comparison-20261028", "schemaVersion": 1, "timestampUtc": "2026-10-28T12:11:22.165315+00:00"}